From 1b396d12378eaf2c799442e4cc31652a0681a158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:54:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic: rtl8365mb: namiltd's RTL8367S-VB (family D) series,
 PR #134

Local copy of the family-D series from namiltd/openwrt#134, head
a6301b8f690406c37ecc4f18ff70ab52f25a1789 (2026-08-27).

Changes since the previous drop (v4, six patches numbered 944-*):
  - renumbered 944-* -> 930-*, because 944-01..04 in backport-6.18 are
    now taken by the devm_mutex_init cleanups that landed upstream;
  - new 930-7: net: dsa: realtek: add family D SDS13 PCS support -
    SGMII/HSGMII PCS for the CPU-facing SerDes, including
    PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX, which is what the AX55 trunk uses.

Verified with target/linux/prepare on the builder's own upstream base
(ax55-618-rebase @785c2661d6, kernel 6.18.39, CONFIG_TESTING_KERNEL=y):
EXIT 0, all seven applied, family-D chip entry and SDS13 PCS present in
the prepared source.
